The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>struct tcf_ife_info {
    // ... other fields ...
    struct list_head metalist;   // list of metaids allowed
};</text>
Reason:
The `metalist` was stored in the action instance (`struct tcf_ife_info`). During a replace operation, new metadata was appended to the existing list instead of replacing it. This caused unbounded growth of the list, eventually leading to an out‑of‑bounds write in `ife_tlv_meta_encode()`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>struct tcf_ife_params {
    // ... other fields ...
    struct list_head metalist;   // list of metaids allowed (rcu-protected)
};</text>
<text>// Removed from struct tcf_ife_info:
//     struct list_head metalist;</text>
Reason:
Moving the `metalist` to the rcu‑protected `tcf_ife_params` ensures that a replace operation creates a new `tcf_ife_params` with a fresh metalist, replacing the old one entirely instead of appending. This prevents unbounded growth and the out‑of‑bounds condition during encoding.

